# K04c: an atom naming a UNIT-LEVEL named Structure is a reference, exactly as a method-local one is
# (unit_valkind_arg_ref_refused), and a number formal refuses it the same way.  Was accepted: the atom typed as
# "unknown" (l2_colon_bound_ty knew own fields, formals, dynamic inputs, slots and machine locals, not a unit
# Structure name), and for an unknown source type the conversion check has nothing to check -- so the generated C
# passed the Structure's descriptor into an int argument and read it there.  See
# defects.md#named-structure-number-argument-typed-unknown.
A:
    int: x 1
end: A

fn: g (int: n) int
    return: n
end: g

fn: m () int
    return: g(A)
end: m

int: r m()
return
